cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Analysis code and processed data for "ARGK-2 sets a transcriptional
  stress response baseline in Caenorhabditis elegans"
message: >-
  If you use this software or data, please cite both the software
  archive and the associated manuscript.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Cole
    family-names: Dunivan
    email: coledunivan@gmail.com
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Biology and Marine Biology, University of North
      Carolina Wilmington, Wilmington, NC, USA
  - given-names: Sarah
    name-particle: R.
    family-names: Fausett
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Biology and Marine Biology, University of North
      Carolina Wilmington, Wilmington, NC, USA
repository-code: 'https://github.com/coledunivan/argk2-cocl2-transcriptomics'
abstract: >-
  Differential expression, functional enrichment, transcription-factor
  target and gene-regulatory-network analysis of a full-factorial bulk
  RNA-seq experiment comparing Caenorhabditis elegans N2, argk-2(ok2723)
  and argk-4(ok3602) under acute CoCl2 oxidative stress, together with
  orthogonal qPCR validation. Reproduces every figure in the associated
  manuscript.
keywords:
  - Caenorhabditis elegans
  - RNA-seq
  - arginine kinase
  - phosphagen kinase
  - oxidative stress
  - cobalt chloride
  - gene-by-environment interaction
  - DESeq2
  - innate immunity
  - mitochondrial retrograde signaling
